{
  "title": "Drop AI offline mode and rely on OpenRouter spend limits instead",
  "description": "The pipeline's AI client supports an `offline=true` mode that \
uses only the local AI cache. This is the default for `make pipeline`, and it \
silently degrades: any time we change the auto-tag prompt, cache keys miss, \
the enrich_auto_tag step returns success=false, and its step output never \
gets written. The pipeline still exits 0 and tag-report.md regenerates as an \
empty table. We hit this while building pipeline snapshots — data/tag-report.md \
went from ~5200 rows to 12 after an offline-mode run and the signal was silent. \
\
Proposal: remove the offline flag and always let enrich_auto_tag call the \
OpenRouter API. Protect against runaway spend via the existing per-key \
OpenRouter spend limit, not via a bespoke cache-only mode. That way prompt \
changes produce fresh cache entries on the next run instead of silently \
poisoning the reports. If we still want a cached-only rerun for debugging, \
make it an explicit flag that errors (rather than silently returning empty) \
on a cache miss.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "ai",
    "pipeline",
  ],
